{"title":"A Sentiment Analysis of Cowen, Hanson, Caplan, and Krugman","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/971171273/0/marginalrevolution~A-Sentiment-Analysis-of-Cowen-Hanson-Caplan-and-Krugman.html","date":1791527195000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.betonit.ai/p/a-sentiment-analysis-of-cowen-hanson?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=820634&amp;post_id=218203389&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\">Supplied by Bryan Caplan</a>, performed by ChatGPT, excerpt:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>So Cowen isn’t well described as either “positive” or “negative.” A much better description is:</p>\r\n<p><strong>High appreciation + high concern + very low emotional agitation.</strong></p>\r\n<p>He seems to think there is an astonishing amount of wonderful stuff in the world <strong>and</strong> an astonishing number of things worth worrying about.</p>\r\n<p>That combination is unusual.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Insightful throughout.  And have a nice day!</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/a-sentiment-analysis-of-cowen-hanson-caplan-and-krugman.html\">A Sentiment Analysis of Cowen, Hanson, Caplan, and Krugman</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/971171273/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/971171273/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/971171273/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/9711712